title: Constitutional Reform
new-page: true
is-card: true
view-if: spd_in_government = 1 and justice_minister_party = "SPD" and constitutional_reform_timer = 0 and judicial_reform >= 2 and constitutional_reform < 3
frequency: 25
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; constitutional_reform_timer += 12; pass_threshold = 0.667
card-image: img/portraits/RadbruchGustav.jpg
go-to: reforms_menu
tags: govt_affairs, cabinet

= Constitutional Reform

The Basic Law has served Germany well since 1949, but many in our party believe that it needs updating. Any change needs a two-thirds majority in both the Bundestag and the Bundesrat, so we will need votes from beyond our own camp.

@reforms_menu

- @vote_threshold: Lower the voting age to 16.
- @constructive_vonc: Introduce nationwide referendums.
- @presidential_powers: Cut off state funding for anti-constitutional parties.
- @as_is: Do not pursue constitutional reform.
- @easy_discard
- @cancel_advisor_action

@vote_threshold
subtitle: Sixteen-year-olds already vote in European elections and in many Länder.
on-arrival: {!
Q.reform_support = Q.spd_normalized + Q.greens_normalized + Q.linke_normalized + Q.fdp_normalized;
if (Q.cdu_relation >= 55) {
    Q.reform_support += Q.cdu_normalized;
}
!}
view-if: voting_age_16 = 0

The Grüne, the Linke and the FDP support it. The Union is against it, saying that the age of majority should stay at eighteen. [? if cdu_relation >= 55 : After long talks, enough of the Union is willing to go along. ?]

- @vote_threshold_2: Put it to the vote!
- @reforms_menu: See other reform options.

@vote_threshold_2
choose-if: reform_support >= pass_threshold
unavailable-subtitle: There is no two-thirds majority for this. [? if cdu_relation < 55 : The Union will not support it. ?]
on-arrival: constitutional_reform += 1; voting_age_16 = 1; cdu_relation -= 3; greens_relation += 3; new_middle_spd += 1; new_middle_greens += 1; new_middle_linke += 1
achievement: verfassungsreform

The Basic Law is amended: from the next election, sixteen-year-olds may vote for the Bundestag.

@constructive_vonc
subtitle: Citizens could put laws to a national vote, as they already can in every Land.
on-arrival: {!
Q.reform_support = Q.spd_normalized + Q.greens_normalized + Q.linke_normalized + Q.bsw_normalized + Q.afd_normalized;
if (Q.cdu_relation >= 60) {
    Q.reform_support += Q.cdu_normalized;
}
!}
view-if: direct_democracy = 0

Referendums at the national level have been an SPD demand for decades. The Grüne, the Linke, the BSW and even the AfD support them, but for very different reasons. The Union and the FDP fear populist campaigns. Some in our own party share that fear.

- @constructive_vonc_2: Put it to the vote!
- @reforms_menu: See other reform options.

@constructive_vonc_2
choose-if: reform_support >= pass_threshold
unavailable-subtitle: There is no two-thirds majority for this. [? if cdu_relation < 60 : The Union will not support it. ?]
on-arrival: constitutional_reform += 1; direct_democracy = 1; democratization += 1; trust_in_democracy += 3; reformist_dissent += 5; afd_relation += 3
achievement: verfassungsreform

The Basic Law is amended: with a million signatures, citizens can now force a national referendum on a law. Most Germans welcome it. Constitutional lawyers warn that the AfD will try to use it against minorities.

@presidential_powers
subtitle: Since 2017, Article 21 allows this, but only through a slow case before the Constitutional Court.
on-arrival: {!
Q.reform_support = Q.spd_normalized + Q.greens_normalized + Q.linke_normalized;
if (Q.cdu_relation >= 40) {
    Q.reform_support += Q.cdu_normalized;
}
if (Q.fdp_relation >= 40) {
    Q.reform_support += Q.fdp_normalized;
}
!}
view-if: presidential_powers = 0

After the NPD case, the Basic Law was changed so that anti-constitutional parties can be cut off from state funding. We propose that the government and the Bundestag can start this process more easily, and that the Verfassungsschutz's rating of a party counts as evidence.

The AfD calls it a plan to silence the opposition. [? if cdu_relation >= 40 : The Union is willing to support it. ?] [? if cdu_relation < 40 : The Union does not trust our motives. ?]

- @presidential_powers_2: Put it to the vote!
- @reforms_menu: See other reform options.

@presidential_powers_2
choose-if: reform_support >= pass_threshold
unavailable-subtitle: There is no two-thirds majority for this. [? if cdu_relation < 40 : The Union will not support it. ?]
on-arrival: constitutional_reform += 1; presidential_powers = 1; afd_relation -= 10; firewall_erosion -= 1 if firewall_erosion > 0; trust_in_democracy += 2
achievement: verfassungsreform

The Basic Law is amended. The AfD's lawyers prepare their challenge in Karlsruhe, and the party's leaders accuse us of fearing the voters.

@as_is
go-to: root
